\par
\tab    If the /V command-line option switch is set, the virtual Slurp\i\par
\i0\tab    format binary loader is used instead of the device-specific\par
\tab    Slurp format\i  \i0 binary loader.  This is a user preference option\par
\tab    (assuming the device-specific Slurp format binary loader is\par
\tab    available); it may be desirable to force usage of the virtual\par
\tab    Slurp format binary loader in certain circumstances.\par
\par
\tab /I If a device-specific Slurp format binary loader is available,\par
\tab    the system device handler is reloaded after all binary files\par
\tab    are loaded.  As a minor restriction, it is not possible to\par
\tab    pass the maximum input file count of 17 input files; the\par
