\tab    effect, the /I command-line option switch is ignored; the\par
\tab    slight restriction on maximum binary input files does not\par
\tab    apply.\par
\par
\tab    If a device-specific Slurp format binary file\i  \i0 loader is in\par
\tab    effect and the /I command-line option switch is not set, the\par
\tab    system device handler will not be available; however, a\par
\tab    device-specific bootstrap will be placed into locations 07600-\par
\tab    07642 to allow program exit to 07600 in a manner consistent\par
\tab    with the system device handler being present.  (Starting the\par
\tab    bootstrap code will reload the P?S/8 keyboard monitor.)\par
\par
\tab    Note: While the starting location of the device-specific\par
\tab    bootstrap is always 07600, the ending address is always\par
\tab    assumed to be the largest case allowed for any and all P?S/8\par
\tab    system configurations (presently 07642); for certain device-\par
\tab    specific bootstraps, this may cause superfluously moving\par
\tab    additional words beyond those actually required to function.\page\tab    Moreover, the largest case allowed is scheduled to be reduced\par
\tab    to 07641 in future releases of P?S/8; this is due to\par
        considerations where the device-specific bootstrap code is\par
\tab    utilized unrelated to binary chaining to P?S/8 BIN from\par
\tab    P?S/8 PAL as discussed in this document.  As of this writing,\par
\tab    the longest existent device-specific bootstrap is slightly\par
\tab    shorter than either the present or planned limit address.\par
\par
\tab    For all systems requiring a system device handler extension,\par
\tab    it is likely (in all future releases of P?S/8), the bootstrap\par
\tab    for all such systems will conform to the following:\line\line\tab\tab CIF\tab x0\tab\tab\tab\tab /CIF TO THE HIGHEST MEMORY FIELD.\par
\tab\tab JMP\tab 7600\tab\tab\tab\tab /CONTINUE THERE.\par
\par
\tab    As such, all systems requiring a system device handler\par
\tab    extension section will produce the smallest bootstrap starting\par
\tab    at 07600.  In these instances, moving additional words will be\par
\tab    irrelevant. (At least one configuration already conforms to\par
\tab    this convention as of P?S/8 Version 8Z.)\par
