\tab    \ul R-L Monitor System\ulnone  Slurp\i  \i0 format binary\i  \i0 loader.  The keyboard\par
\tab    monitor commands were modified to be consistent with the\par
\tab    proposed COS systems released somewhat later.\page\cf2 Glossary of Terms (continued)\par
\cf0\par
\tab    Note: Early releases of P?S/8 are faithful to the original\par
\tab    keyboard monitor commands of the \ul R-L Monitor System\ulnone ; however,\par
\tab    all recent releases are consistent with the DIBOL/COS systems.\par
\tab    Where relevant, documentation of the COS keyboard commands\par
\tab    also applies to P?S/8.\par
\par
\tab c) \ul\i POLY BASIC\ulnone\i0  is a stand-alone BASIC-only operating system for a\par
\tab    4K PDP-8 including any of several storage devices such as the\par
\tab    TC01/TC08 DECtape, PDP-12 LINCtape, DF32 and RF08.  The \ul POLY\par
\ulnone\tab    \ul BASIC\ulnone  source code was originally created on The \ul R-L Monitor\par
\ulnone\tab    \ul System\ulnone  by the same students who created the original \ul R-L\par
\ulnone\tab    \ul Monitor System\ulnone  while students (just before their employment\par
\tab    began at DEC in Maynard Mass).\par
\par
\tab    Note: Since \ul POLY BASIC\ulnone  is a standalone operating system,\par
\tab    binary output from PAL III is loaded into memory; when the\par
\tab    system halts, a scratch DECtape is mounted on drive unit 0 to\par
